  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Sun Jul 19 2026\n\nThe beginning and middle of the work weeks are a bit complicated \nwith multiple hazards at the same time. Tuesday into Wednesday, a \n500mb trough and accompanying low pressure system will swing through \nOntario, dragging behind them the cold front we will see Tuesday \nnight into Wednesday. This will bring us some forcing and not \nsurprisingly, a risk for severe weather. SPC has seen this setup in \nthe guidance and put us in a Day 3 slight risk (level 2 out of 5) \nfor severe weather. As it stands now, damaging winds continue their \nstreak of being a popular hazard with our severe chances this \nsummer. There appears to be a low end tornado threat in CAMs with \nthis system, with a linear storm mode to boot. Something we will \nhave to keep an eye on in future forecast packages. In addition to \nthe severe risk, heat indices will be dangerously high on Tuesday, \nexceeding 105 in quite a few areas west of the plateau. \n\nAfter the cold front, we will enter a quieter period for the mid-\nweek. Highs will be in the mid 80s starting on Wednesday, slowly \nwarming back into the 90s into next weekend. It does look like we \ncould see another system Friday into Friday night associated with a \nshortwave in the mid-levels, but specifics are not too clear on that \nsystem just yet.",
